##DESCRIPTION
##  Statistics problem: confidence intervals
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Hypothesis tests)
## DBsection(Independent samples - t)
## Date(11/04/2012)
## Institution(UBC)
## Author(Djun Kim)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('statistics', 'statistical inference', 'hypothesis test', 'p-value', 'interpretatin')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',         'PGML.pl',
    'parserCheckboxList.pl', 'parserMultiAnswer.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

($x0, $x1) = (random(-1, -0.1, 0.1), random(1.5, 6.5, 0.1));

$cb = CheckboxList(
    [
        [
            'A two-sided two-sample test for a difference between the two population means '
                . 'is not rejected at the 10% significance level.',
            'A two-sided paired test for a difference between the two population means is '
                . 'not rejected at the 10% significance level.',
            'A two-sided paired test for a difference between the two population means is '
                . 'rejected at the 10% significance level.',
            'A two-sided two-sample test for a difference between the two population means '
                . 'is rejected at the 10% significance level.',
        ],
        'None of the Above'
    ],
    [0],
    labels => 'ABC'
);

BEGIN_PGML
A 90% confidence interval for the difference between the means of two independent populations is found to be [`([$x0],[$x1])`].

Which of the following statements is/are correct? CHECK ALL THAT APPLY. [_]{$cb}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The only correct statement is [$cb].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT(); 